WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:02.929
Put on your deerstalker and load up your pipe.

00:00:02.929 --> 00:00:06.100
It's time to determine the facts of the latest
Sherlock Holmes case.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:07.060
"Is it a cap?

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:07.940
Why's it got two fronts?"

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:08.940
"It's a deerstalker."

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:15.020
A report from We Got This Covered indicates
that Robert Downey Jr. and Jude Law's Sherlock

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:20.110
Holmes and Dr. Watson will return to face
an American nemesis named Senator Cornelius

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:24.510
Guest, a man obsessed with stealing gold,
in the third installment of the big-screen

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:25.900
Sherlock Holmes franchise.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:29.720
A villain obsessed with gold in the third
installment of a franchise?

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:30.220
Huh.

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:31.500
That sounds familiar.

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:35.340
"I love goooooold!"

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:40.680
Anyway, they'll possibly be traveling to the
United States to take on the gold-obsessed

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:41.360
Senator.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:46.539
HN Entertainment first reported the rumor
back in March 2019 that Holmes and Watson

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:48.680
will be going to San Francisco, specifically.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:53.040
Official word on the project is scarce, as
it's been languishing in pre-production for

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:58.460
close to a decade due to Robert Downey Jr.'s
rather crowded schedule full of Marvel projects.

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:03.300
The time is now ripe for speculation, though,
as production is slated to begin in January

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:03.920
2020.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:09.100
So will we see the immortal detective visit
the Wild Wild West for our viewing pleasure?

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:10.340
The game is afoot.

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:14.920
The fact of the matter is that there is nothing
to disprove nor confirm the rumor.

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:19.909
It's entirely possible that the name "Senator
Cornelius Guest" is a cover to maintain secrecy,

00:01:19.909 --> 00:01:25.240
and it's worth mentioning that Sherlock Holmes:
A Game of Shadows included the iconic Reichenbach

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:30.900
Falls scenario also featured in the BBC's
Sherlock series in which Holmes and his arch-nemesis

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:33.480
Professor Moriarty are both presumed dead.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:38.640
The scenario was inspired by Sir Arthur Conan
Doyle's Holmes tale "The Final Problem."

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:43.200
In that story and most of its adaptations,
the detective always survives, while Moriarty

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.250
isn't so lucky.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:48.500
But one shouldn't immediately assume that
Game of Shadows' version of the character,

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:50.420
played by Jared Harris, couldn't return.

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:52.140
"That doesn't bode well, does it?"

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:57.939
The Sherlock Holmes 3 script has passed through
many, many hands in the years that RDJ has

00:01:57.939 --> 00:02:02.820
been occupied in the Iron Man suit, so all
bets are off as to exactly where it's going

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:03.660
to land, plot-wise.

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:08.280
It's quite possible that a draft brought Holmes
to America, but is it the final one?

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:12.940
Nothing is certain until new director Dexter
Fletcher or Warner Bros. makes an official

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:13.440
announcement.

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:18.240
To the casual eye reviewing the rumor, it
might feel a touch like it's blowing up the

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:23.120
concept to have the English detective appear
in America, dealing with an American antagonist.

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:28.640
Arthur Conan Doyle never sent Holmes to America
on a case, but it is implied that after throwing

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:34.010
himself off of Reichenbach Falls with Moriarty,
he spent some time overseas before coming

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:36.340
back to give Watson the shock of his life.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:41.860
And Doyle's first Holmes novel, A Study In
Scarlet, features several American characters

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:45.380
and an extended flashback of their lives within
the Mormon church in Utah.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:50.400
Doyle had a personal fascination with the
U.S., and cited famous American detective

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:54.180
and friend William J. Burns as "the American
Sherlock Holmes."

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:58.540
Holmes' last name is itself a nod to American
poet Oliver Wendell Holmes.

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:03.270
Guy Ritchie, the director of the first two
films in the series, never seemed interested

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:06.220
in directly adapting Doyle's Holmes stories.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:10.660
Both his films cherry picked the characters
we were most likely to recognize and remixed

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:12.620
them with semi-historical context.

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:17.540
For example, the first flick's villain, Lord
Blackwood, seems like an off-brand version

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:18.440
of Jack the Ripper.

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:22.460
Ritchie's films also winkingly referenced
the life of Doyle himself.

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:27.260
Holmes paid the bills for Doyle and ultimately
made him very wealthy, but he never loved

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:28.440
Holmes the way the public did.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:33.470
He was forever bitter that his books about
history, fairies, and spiritualism — his

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:37.260
true passions — were nowhere near as popular
as his detective stories.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:42.280
Ritchie incorporated a lot of occult concepts
and historical remixes into these stories

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:46.210
as his own kind of homage, which might have
been lost on viewers who hadn't read much

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:47.300
of Doyle's other work.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:49.440
"There was never any magic!

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:52.900
Only conjuring tricks!"

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:57.680
We're going to go ahead and categorize this
product of the rumor mill as a firm "maybe."

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:02.120
Of course, once official news breaks about
the plot, setting and title of Sherlock Holmes

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:05.500
3, we'll be here to investigate every clue.

